  "workflow_name": "Electron-phonon coupling analysis from optical spectra of solid-state defects",
  "definition": "This workflow analyzes low-temperature optical spectra (photoluminescence, absorption, or excitation) of point defects or impurity centers in solids to quantify electron-phonon coupling. It involves identifying the zero-phonon line (ZPL), measuring vibronic sidebands, and extracting the Huang-Rhys factor S, dominant phonon energy ℏω, and stabilization energy from spectral features using methods such as Poisson distribution fitting or intensity ratio relations.",
